---
fmContentType: glossaryEntry
term: "Hemp"
letter: "H"
anchor: "hemp"
category: "general"
---

Cannabis plants legally defined as containing 0.3% THC or less by dry weight. Hemp is federally legal in the US under the 2018 Farm Bill. Hemp is grown for CBD extraction, fibre, seeds, and other industrial uses. Hemp flower can be used in the same home infusion processes as cannabis flower — producing CBD-dominant infusions with negligible THC.
